Sable Embertail <EXECUTOR> — #327 bboxy450-term test sweep

Scope: app tests/cfg(test), the smallest model clock seam, and append-only exact night selectors (Oracle618e403c and standing3c2df395). Inventory: current-source cargo -- --list,333 tests, no unmapped entries.226 reviewed;107 peer-owned rows deliberately unchanged (including the already accepted Rook lifecycle/custody cut).

Mechanisms:
- model::build keeps its normal clock read in the original location; build_at supplies explicit monotonic/wall coordinates. Close/model/frame fixtures use deadline61000 at wall1000. The clock-bypass mutation failed the close assertions and the original source hash was restored.
- Live IO test publications signal Notify via the real DirtySet wake. The fixture drains the DirtySet and checks the retained Model before waiting, eliminating the10ms polling loop. Removed three unobserved fixed delays. Notify coalescing and cancellation now inspect Pending directly.
- Recovery ACK backpressure uses a ListSeats reply barrier instead of a250ms negative timeout. Cancellation tests poll the retained future once; positive asynchronous waits keep guards of at least30s.
- Public snapshot, typed terminal results, generated pane controls, pane bounds and rim paint replace private queue/map/rim/swell checks. Real boundary checks preserve state, pixels, ordering, ownership, output and exactness assertions.
- Removed no_launcher_paint_proof (A2): printed paint bytes were not asserted, and its only assertion pinned the fixture pane count. retained_launcher_hit_regions_and_unwrapped_foreground_order checks the actual paint output and ordering.
-40 exact named boundary selectors appended; no blanket --ignored. The old selector prefix is byte-identical. All40 passed: prior R5+night runner2/0, headless17/0 and remaining IO/recovery/CLI21/0. Existing lifecycle/custody selectors unchanged.
-4 sleep calls removed (live.rs); the16s recovery sleep uses start_paused. Remaining short observation polls exist only in retained real-boundary night fixtures. No speed threshold was added.

Verification (raw logs retained privately; paths and hashes in manifest):
- app-controlled-close-tests: EXIT0,7/0; clock-bypass mutation cargo EXIT101 as expected, source restored; mutation driver EXIT0.
- app-sweep-library-tests: EXIT0,80/0; app-sweep-settings-tests: EXIT0,8/0.
- app-headless-night-validation: EXIT0,17/0; app-remaining-night-validation-fixed-2: EXIT0,21/0.
- app-sweep-live-unit-check: EXIT0,20/0,3 intentionally ignored boundary cases.
- Initial remaining-boundary compilation failed E0609 because Context has no rim field; fixed to inspect actual pane layout. An accidental missing private driver launch exited2 and performed no test. Strengthened scene paint checks initially rejected two arbitrary fixture IDs at the shader seed validator; those fixtures now use a bounded deterministic seat ID. These red logs are retained.
- app-rewritten-unit-validation-fixed: EXIT0; scene17/0 and notification recording/worker6/0. Author presubmit pending in this source commit; successor evidence records its actual result.

